{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"downy-feminist-leopard","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Summary\n\nAutodeploy deploys container components but **never** re-renders `/etc/nginx/conf.d/rebar.conf`. The edge is not \"skipped because a delta was missed\" — its source template is absent from **every** component path manifest in `infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh`, so a delta can never be detected. Any merged change to the nginx edge stays permanently un-live until a human applies it by hand.\n\n## Evidence (live box i-00880b2c7f13527c5)\n\nThe complete manifest set in `/opt/rebar/infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh`:\n\n```\n172:BOT_PATHS='src/rebar/ infra/compose/Dockerfile.reviewbot pyproject.toml infra/compose/docker-compose.yml infra/scripts/reviewbot-ensure-tickets.sh'\n179:SECRETS_PATHS='infra/scripts/fetch-secrets.sh infra/terraform/ssm.tf'\n184:MCP_PATHS='src/rebar infra/compose/Dockerfile.mcp infra/compose/docker-compose.yml uv.lock pyproject.toml'\n194:CONFIG_PATHS='infra/gerrit/replication.config infra/gerrit/project.config infra/gerrit/gerrit_to_platform.ini.template infra/gerrit/materialize-g2p-config.sh infra/compose/gerrit.config'\n198:OBS_PATHS='infra/scripts/observability.sh infra/scripts/install-observability.sh'\n203:CERTBOT_PATHS='infra/scripts/install-certbot-timer.sh'\n```\n\nThe edge source of truth is `/opt/rebar/infra/nginx/rebar.conf.template` (the only file in `infra/` containing `proxy_redirect`). It appears in **none** of the six manifests. There is no `NGINX_PATHS` / `EDGE_PATHS`.\n\nThe **only** nginx write autodeploy performs is the MCP blue-green pointer swap against a *separate* materialized include:\n\n```\n160:MCP_UPSTREAM_FILE=\"${MCP_UPSTREAM_FILE:-/etc/nginx/mcp-upstream.conf}\"  # materialized nginx /mcp/ include\n528:# Atomically re-point the /mcp/ upstream include at $1 (a host port) and reload nginx.\n```\n\nThat swap touches `mcp-upstream.conf` and reloads nginx; it never regenerates `rebar.conf`. This precisely explains the observed split: the 23:21 deploy moved the MCP container to `rebar-mcp-25ea12c200ae-8092` (upstream include rewritten, reload issued) while `rebar.conf` stayed untouched.\n\nConfirming state:\n\n```\n/etc/nginx/conf.d/rebar.conf mtime=2026-08-27 22:05:26 +0000\nproxy_redirect count = 7\n```\n\nAug 27 22:05 predates the 2026-08-28 23:21 deploy, and 7 `proxy_redirect` directives is the pre-`a61d` shape (79b2's three rules), not `a61d`'s six sibling rules plus three restated defaults. So change `25fd2cf6dd75` is merged but not live, and cannot become live by itself.\n\nAlso observed (may be unrelated cadence/backoff, noted for the investigator): `/var/lib/rebar/deployed-sha` = `ae203145fa39a153c21b6cba8b25cb5679849ec9` while the mirror's `origin/main` = `565e1856bc9d180876fdbcaa336ccd57ceb8202e`.\n\n## Why this matters beyond one stale rule\n\nThis falsifies the standing assumption — recorded on `enchanting-phantastic-weevil` (a61d-adf9-3725-4847) — that the edge fix \"will land without manual intervention once the deferral clears\". The deferral cleared and the containers deployed; the edge did not, and never will under the current manifest. Every future edge change inherits the same silent no-op.\n\nNote that story `gall-plume-adder` (8903) scoped v1 auto-apply to the review-bot container only, with Gerrit config as detect-only. The nginx edge was not enumerated in either category, so it does not even get the `AUTODEPLOY_ERROR` detect-and-signal treatment that `CONFIG_PATHS` receives — it fails **silently**.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `infra/nginx/rebar.conf.template` (and any other edge input) is enumerated in an autodeploy path manifest, so a change to it is detected.\n- [ ] A detected edge change is either applied (render template -> `nginx -t` -> `nginx -s reload`, with rollback to the prior conf on `nginx -t` failure) or, at minimum, signalled via `AUTODEPLOY_ERROR` the way `CONFIG_PATHS` is — never silently ignored.\n- [ ] Applying the edge never restarts or otherwise touches the `gerrit` container; blast radius is the nginx config plus a reload.\n- [ ] A malformed rendered conf fails `nginx -t` and is rolled back, leaving the previous working edge serving; `deployed-sha` is not advanced.\n- [ ] Proven live: a merged edge change reaches `/etc/nginx/conf.d/rebar.conf` with no manual step, evidenced by an mtime advance and the new directive set present.\n- [ ] `enchanting-phantastic-weevil` (a61d) is unblocked — its merged change `25fd2cf6dd75` is verified live at the edge.\n","id":"1d1b-a719-b675-4a1f","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Autodeploy never re-renders the nginx edge: infra/nginx/rebar.conf.template is in no component path manifest, so edge changes can never go live"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787960874868631281,"uuid":"7cb40f27-3d06-4eac-b727-59c9281fd429"}